{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791631301,"nonce":"yYdxjvdwldN2xbteEVRXgKwDZbM=","message":"Cause: note_hot_loop tried the late OSR entry only on a header's first notification. On the Mac that notification came before a tick had made the function's compiled code visible in the entry table, and the header was already in hot_loops, so the entry was never attempted again.\n\nFix: c1fa78dde6fda7fbb36ab3f247b8927c6763a51b on branch perf-queue, not on main yet. A header whose code is not visible yet stays pending, and its late entry is attempted on the first later notification after the code is.\n\nCheck, Mac arm64, the command above with the fixed build: 8 runs, 8 of 8 print `[osr] entering` once and `[retier] taken` once, each with iters=3000000 nulls=3000000 back=0 last=2999999. Before the fix, three runs each gave 1/0/1 taken lines on the base build and 1/0/0 on the perf-queue build without the retry.\n\n`cargo test --release -p ash --test osr_retier`: 5 of 5 in three passes in a row, forced_snapshots_from_ordinary_and_osr_entries_preserve_live_state among them, with the machine at load average about 43.\n\nLeaving this open until perf-queue is on main.","files":null}]}